		(uuid "aba3b593-ef67-45da-b73b-ce08d23a89dd")
	)
	(text "(1) USB-C into RP2040-Zero port (5V)\n     The default configuration powers/programs the SAO\n     Demo Controller RP2040-Zero regardless of the\n     power switch position. The USB 5V is also routed\n     to the LiPo battery charge IC.\n     POWER SWITCH ON = downstream SAO is powered.\n     POWER SWITCH OFF = downstream SAO is not powered.\n\n(2) External battery, 2-4 AA/AAA or 1S LiPo/LiPoly \n     (A) The default configuration is for non-rechargeable\n     Primary/Alkaline cells with both the charger and LiPo\n     protector disabled. Allowed input is 3 to 16 V per\n     limits of Buck-Boost 3.3V Converter.\n     Practically, 3 to 8 \"AA\" or \"AAA\" batteries may be used\n     including non-rechargeable Lithium-Iron Disulfide (Li-FeS₂)\n     consumer batteries such as Energizer Ultimate Lithium\n     which may offer up to 1.8V per cell when fresh.\n     A variety of coil cells may be used as long as they can\n     deliver enough current and do not exceed 16V.\n     \n     (B) Optionally, to use a 1S LiPo/LiPoly cell verify\n     the connection polarity to JST-PH BATT. port. (Adafruit)\n     POWER SWITCH ON = RP2040-Zero and SAO are powered.\n     POWER SWITCH OFF = RP2040-Zero and SAO are not powered.\n\n(3) SAO input port 3.3V expected, 2 to 6V allowed\n     (A) The default configuration expects power to be supplied\n     through the SAO port from the badge or host. As such,\n     solder jumper SJ_REV_PWR_BDG \"Reverse Power Badge\"\n     is open by default.\n     \n     (B) As long as the badge/host does NOT have it's own\n     power source, you may optionally provide 3.3V to the\n     badge/host, AKA \"reverse powering it\" by removing \n     reverse protection diode D4 and closing solder\n     jumper SJ_REV_PWR_BDG. In this configuration, power is\n     provided from your external battery or USB C into the\n     RP2040-Zero through the 3.3V Buck-Boost Converter and \n     into your badge or host device.\n\nDiodes prevent backfeeding between four input power\noptions. Diodes may be removed and solder-bridged to\nimprove efficiency if you make sure you don't create\na backfeed power issue between the three sources.\n\nAll power sources, with the exception of the USB-C \n5V, flow through a switch for convenience. If USB-C\npower is supplied, the battery charger and RP2040-Zero\nwill always be powered. The switch enables/disables\nthe 3.3V Buck/Boost Converter. SO YOUR SAO WILL NOT GET\nPOWER UNLESS THAT SWITCH IS ON AS WELL!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.224 142.748 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b60f75bf-8463-4342-ac98-049086b679e8")
	)
